<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 45 M3 follow-up: A MASTER INSERT MADE WHILE A LANE IS ALREADY
  MONITORING MUST REBUILD THE LIVE PLAN.

  Found while gating M3 and named in PR #171 as not fixed. Every other master
  gate in this suite builds the master chain BEFORE arming, so the plan is
  correct on its first publication and nothing rebuilds it. This case is the
  one that arms first and edits the master afterwards, which is the ordinary
  user gesture: monitor a take, then drop a limiter on the master.

  WHAT WAS WRONG. SLiveMonitor has exactly one rebuild trigger for an edit that
  does not change the live SET: the 40 ms pumpEdits() tick, which republishes
  when planSignature() differs. That signature walks `current_.ordered`, the
  CLOSURE MEMBERS, and the master lane is deliberately not one of them (D2: a
  master lane is not a childLinks() member). So a master insert, a master fader
  move, a master mute and a master automation lane were ALL invisible to it: the
  live plan kept whatever master shape it was built with, for the life of the
  arm.

  It is not a cosmetic staleness. Under the LINEAR split the RT adds the frozen
  root page to the ring, and the FREEZE path does apply the new master insert
  while the ring bypasses it, so the two halves stop belonging to the same
  signal. That is exactly the mismatch D4a's shape check exists to prevent, and
  it went undetected because nothing re-asked the question.

  THE MEASUREMENT is the M3 ring-only discriminator, run a second time with the
  master insert applied LATE:

    master_closure_linear_ring   ring alone, no master     0.082071
    master_closure_heard_ring    ring alone, 2.0x master   0.164142   (built early)
    THIS CASE                    ring alone, 2.0x master   0.164142   (built LATE)

  Pre-fix this reads the FIRST row, because the plan is still the one published
  at arm time. The two bands are disjoint by a factor of two.

  THE WINDOW AND THE FIXTURE ARE master_closure_heard_ring's, unchanged, and
  the reasoning for both is in that case's header: the sources are uncorrelated
  (root test_autosaw.wav, ring test_sawtooth.wav), the armed track runs through
  a 0.25 gain so the 2.0x master does not clip a 16-bit capture, the fixture is
  placed twice for 8 s, and [168000, 216000) is the one window that is past the
  monitor priming lag AND inside the material.

  THE INSERT LANDS AT ROUGHLY 2.6 s of captured audio, which is past the
  priming lag and 0.9 s before the window opens. That margin covers the 40 ms
  rebuild tick and the RT's crossfade at the flip with an order of magnitude to
  spare; it is not tuned to them.

  THE LOG ASSERTION IS A PAIR, and that is not belt and braces. The string
  "the RT pops the ring only" appears in SLiveMonitor's Closure line AND is
  interpolated by the plan builder, which is what made the retired
  master_insert_refuses_monitoring vacuous. So the Closure sentence being
  PRESENT is asserted together with the refusal sentence being ABSENT, and the
  audio is measured independently of both.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="master_insert_while_monitoring">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <!-- Track 0: armed and monitored, on the paced file input carrying
         test_sawtooth.wav (RMS 0.328284), through a 0.25 gain = 0.082071. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-input trackPath="0" input="audio:file:3"/>
    <set-monitor-mode trackPath="0" mode="on"/>
    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gain"
                   name="Smaragd Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="0.25"/>

    <!-- Track 1: NEVER armed, and held at -60 dB so this case measures the
         RING alone. Placed twice for 8 s of material. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="1" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="1" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="192000"/>
    <set-track-volume trackPath="1" volume="-60"/>

    <!-- ARM AND ROLL WITH A CLEAN MASTER. The plan published here is LINEAR,
         and every other master gate in this suite stops caring at this point. -->
    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="1"/>
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>

    <!-- Past the priming lag, with the lane live and the transport rolling. -->
    <wait-ms ms="2600"/>

    <!-- THE GESTURE UNDER TEST. Nothing here touches the live SET, so the only
         thing that can notice is the signature tick. -->
    <insert-plugin trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gain"
                   name="Smaragd Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="2.0"/>

    <wait-ms ms="2600"/>

    <!-- THE PLAN REBUILT AS A CLOSURE, AND MONITORING WAS NOT REFUSED, both
         asserted INSIDE the window opened by the wait above. assert-log's
         window starts at the immediately preceding action that is not itself
         an assert-log, so this pair reads exactly the 2.6 s that follow the
         master edit, not the whole run. Placed at the end of the case, after
         dump-playback-capture, they would have read the DUMP's window and
         found nothing, which is how the first draft of this case failed. -->
    <assert-log level="warn" contains="the RT pops the ring only" minCount="1"/>
    <assert-log level="warn" contains="live monitoring is off"
                minCount="0" maxCount="0"/>

    <toggle-playback play="0"/>

    <dump-playback-capture filename="master_insert_while_monitoring.wav" minFrames="216000"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="master_insert_while_monitoring.wav"
                         startFrame="168000" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.1592" maxRms="0.1691"/>

    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="0"/>

    <!-- AC3.4: the late flip into Closure must not put a freeze worker on the
         master lane's own processor instances. -->
    <assert-render-policy liveThreadRefusals="0" liveOwnedRefusals="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
